  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.6.2 refuses two mistakes it used to mishandle: text compared with a number it cannot be read as, and instants a nanosecond timestamp cannot reach.\n\n      - **Text beside a number:** `qty = 'x'`, where `qty` is a number, is refused while the statement is validated, at the text, coded `SqlValidation`, rather than failing as a planner `Internal` error. The same holds for `<>`, the orderings, `IN`, `NOT IN` and `BETWEEN`. Text that reads as the number, `qty = '1.5'`, stands.\n      - **Text beside a time:** `ts = '2026-01-08 12:00:00+02:00'`, which failed with the same internal error, now runs: ChalkQL's cast reads the text when the statement runs, and names any it cannot read.\n      - **Nanosecond timestamps:** a .NET time converted to a nanosecond timestamp is refused if it falls before 1677-09-21 or after 2262-04-11, where it wrapped into a wrong instant.\n      - **Compatibility:** no change to the API, the protocol or the IR. A 0.6.1 planner serves a 0.6.2 client, without the new refusals.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.6.2",
